<title>AUSTRALIA: Cricket-Australia beat West Indies by 123 runs.</title>
<headline>Cricket-Australia beat West Indies by 123 runs.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia beat West Indies by 123 runs on the final day of the first test at the Gabba on Tuesday.</p>
<p>West Indies, chasing 420 to win, were bowled out for 296 with 14.1 overs left. Kenneth Benjamin was the last wicket to fall, leg before wicket to Glenn McGrath for one.</p>
<p>The tourists lost their last three wickets for three runs.</p>
<p>Opener Sherwin Campbell top-scored for West Indies with 113.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
